<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec trade surplus falls 20.6 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec trade surplus falls 20.6 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus fell 20.6 percent in December from a year ago to 881.48 billion yen, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The merchandise trade surplus with the United States, often a source of trade friction, rose 7.8 percent to 389.11 billion yen in December from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The figures were not adjusted for seasonal factors.  </p>
